{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ columbia hamilton hall ida gym 1968)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_3164994015#4_3495004671","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3850","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_3164994015#4_3495004671\" , \"end_char\": 6022.000000 , \"headings\": \"Columbia University protests of 1968 Columbia University protests of <cover>1968 Contents Background Discovery of IDA documents Morningside Park gymnasium Protests Occupation of Hamilton Hall Activist separation Popular responses Suppression of protesters Second round of protests Aftermath Immediate responses Long term effects In popular culture See also References Further reading External links \" , \"segment\": \"Due to the topography of the area, Columbia's campus at Morningside Heights to the west was more than 100 feet (30 m) above the adjacent neighborhood of Harlem to the east. The proposed design would have an upper level to be used as a Columbia gym, </cover>and a lower level to be used as a community center. By 1968, concerned students and community members saw the planned separate east and west entrances as an attempt to circumvent the Civil Rights Act of 1964, then a recent federal law that banned racially segregated facilities. In addition, others were concerned with the appropriation of land from a public park. Harlem activists opposed ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_3164994015#5_3495006769","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_3164994015#6_3495009430","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
